# Week 6 Learning Journal – Team Project Setup

**Date:** 18 July 2026

## Overview

This week focused on preparing for the group project. Our team set up the communication and collaboration tools that will be used throughout the semester. We organised our project environment and made sure every team member had access to the required platforms.

## What I Learned

During this week's activities, I learned how to use several collaboration tools for software development:

- Joined the team's Slack workspace for communication.
- Connected with my teammates on LinkedIn.
- Joined the GitHub repository for version control.
- Learned how to use GitHub for sharing and managing project files.
- Joined the team's Trello board to organise tasks and monitor project progress.

I also learned the importance of using version control and project management tools when working as part of a development team.

## Practical Work

This week I completed the following tasks:

- Joined my team's Slack channel.
- Connected with teammates on LinkedIn.
- Joined the GitHub Classroom repository.
- Accessed the team's Trello board.
- Reviewed the project plan and group agreement.
